Sally</span>: Vanessa, I've decided - I'm going to go on a diet.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh, seriously? Why now?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Well, I drink 5-6 cups of coffee everyday, and I eat too much fast food."}, {"time": "12200", "image": "engenn6le03ob10re2img06.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yeah, you're going to have to stop eating so much if you want to feel healthy.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: For sure. I'm going to have to eat more nutritious foods to not gain any more weight. I even used to be vegetarian. Now I like meat.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: And you don't have to eat just a little bit or eat only salads. You've just gotta make better choices in what you consume.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hmmm, tell me more."}, {"time": "34200", "image": "engenn6le03ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You see, you've got to eat foods with protein and fiber to keep you full longer. Reduce your calories to 1500, and have a good portion of fruits and veggies with every meal. Some have good antioxidants too.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: So, I can still ingest exciting foods.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yeah, and desserts aren't against the law. Just watch your portions.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Alright. I'll commence on the journey tomorrow."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa: Dinner for Four"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Time for a Diet"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Identify and describe personal and regional eating habits and cooking in a range of communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le03ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Expressing Quantities and Amounts"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are many expressions used to express large amounts in English. In general, <span class=\"strong\">much</span> and <span class=\"strong\">many</span> are the standard quantifiers used to express large quantities.<br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Much</span> is used with <span class=\"italic\">uncountable nouns</span>:<br><br> <span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span><br> <span class=\"italic\">There is much interest in learning English around the world.<br>\u2028How much money do you have?<br>\u2028There isn't much butter left in the refrigerator</span>.<br><br> <span class=\"strong\">Many</span> is used with <span class=\"italic\">countable nouns</span>:<br><br> <span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span><br> <span class=\"italic\">There are many people who use the computer every day.<br>\u2028How many students live close to the school?<br>\u2028There aren't many books on that shelf.</span><br><br> The following expressions are often used in place of <span class=\"strong\">much</span> and <span class=\"strong\">many</span>, especially in positive sentences.<br><br> a lot of<br>\u2028lots of<br>\u2028plenty of<br>\u2028a great deal of<br>\u2028a large number of<br>\u2028the majority of<br>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I eat too much fast food."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I had too many slices of pizza last night."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I must drink a lot of water."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Saying what is NOT necessary"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use \"<span class=\"strong\">Don't have to</span>\" or \"<span class=\"strong\">Doesn't have to</span>\" to express what is not necessary. <br/>Remember to use a verb in its base form after \"<span class=\"strong\">Don't</span>/<span class=\"strong\">Doesn't have to</span>\"."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject <br/>You/We/I/They <br/>She/He </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">+ auxiliary in negative<br/><span class=\\\"strong\\\">don't <br/>doesn't</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span> to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ verb in base form (infinitive)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ complement\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You <span class=\"strong\">don't</span> <span class=\"italic\">have</span> to eat just a little bit or eat only salads. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> <span class=\"italic\">have</span> to watch her portions."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "healthy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to eat food or live in a way that's good for your health "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to stop eating so much if you want to be healthy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear/use when talking about diets."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to gain weight"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a more polite way to talk about increase in weight"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sally would have to eat more nutritious foods to not gain weight."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "protein"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a substance found in milk, eggs, meat and beans that helps the body to grow and be strong "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Foods with more protein are important to make your muscles strong."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fiber"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "vegetable material that cannot be digested and help other food to pass through your body "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Foods with more fiber help to clear your system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "calorie"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a measurement used to indicate the amount of energy that foods will produce in the human body "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Each of us should eat enough to get 1500-2000 calories a day."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "antioxidant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a substance contained in certain foods that prevents some chemicals from damaging our body "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Blueberries and broccoli contain a lot of antioxidants."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob10aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to ingest"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to eat or swallow"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Ingesting a lot deep-fried foods is not unhealthy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob10aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think about everything you eat each day and how your diet can improve. Write down some notes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 5 sentences using expressions of necessity on how you plan to make your diet more nutritious."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Be sure to also include quantities and amounts in your sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your new diet plan to your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I apply critical-thinking to my eating habits."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write complete statements on how my diet can improve."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I expression necessity and quantities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my new diet plan to my partner."}]}]}